'faqs'=>[['Can an autistic girl have close friends?','Yes. Friendship does not exclude autism. Clinicians consider how relationships are formed and maintained, how much effort they require and whether misunderstandings repeatedly occur.'],['Can good grades hide autism?','Yes. Academic achievement measures only part of functioning. Sensory overload, social confusion, organisation difficulties and exhaustion may remain hidden behind strong grades.'],['Is masking the same as pretending?','Masking is often an adaptive response to social expectations or stigma. It may be conscious or automatic and can require substantial concentration and energy.'],['Who can assess autism in a teenage girl?','Seek clinicians trained in adolescent autism and varied presentations. A comprehensive assessment should include developmental history, multiple settings, direct observation and the teenager&rsquo;s own experience.']],
